# ACT ONE

= A windbound evening. Two old friends and a lamp that won'tstay lit.

## SCENE 1

A single oil lamp on a wooden table, centre stage. ELENAsits beside it,reading. The light flickers. Outside, a wind that has beenblowing forthree days is somehow louder now.

ELENA
(without looking up)
You're back early.

MARCUS enters from the wings, brushing snow from his coat.

MARCUS
The road's closed past the bridge.
ELENA
Then sit down before you melt on the carpet.

MARCUS sits opposite her. The lamp gutters. Both look at it,then ateach other.

ELENA
Don't.
MARCUS
I haven't done anything.
ELENA
You were about to.

A long pause. The wind eases for a moment, and in the gapMARCUS speaksmore quietly than he means to.

MARCUS
I had a letter today.
ELENA
(turning a page)
From whom.
MARCUS
You know from whom.

ELENA closes the book. She does not look at him.

ELENA
What did it say.
MARCUS
That she's well. That she's coming back in thespring. That she would
like to see us. Both of us.

= Elena considers throwing the book.

ELENA
"Both of us."
MARCUS
That's what it said.

The lamp goes out completely. Neither of them moves. After amomentELENA strikes a match. The light comes back, smaller thanbefore.

## SCENE 2

The lamp has gone out again, properly this time. ELENA isalone, standingat the window. The wind has stopped. The silence is worse.

ELENA
(to the dark)
I knew you would.

She does not turn when MARCUS enters quietly behind her.

MARCUS
Knew I would what.
ELENA
Write back.

A beat.

MARCUS
I haven't yet.
ELENA
But you will.

He doesn't answer. She finally turns.

ELENA
I'm not asking you to choose.
MARCUS
I know.
ELENA
I'm telling you that you already have.

Lights fade.

# ACT TWO

= Same room. The thaw, and what it brings up out of theground.

## SCENE 1

The same room, mid-morning. Sunlight where there has beennone for threedays. ELENA pours tea for one. The lamp is still on thetable, unlit,spotless. There is no sign of MARCUS.

She lifts the cup. She does not drink.

ELENA
(softly)
Alright.

A KNOCK at the door. She does not move.

ELENA
(to herself)
Alright.

Another knock. She sets the cup down without spilling it andcrossesto the door. She does not open it.

ELENA
(through the door)
Tell her the road's open now.

She returns to the table and sits in MARCUS's chair.

End of play.
